Before: GET /courses/crs_42 returned
{"id":"crs_42","title":"HTTP Basics","level":"beginner","price":149000,"prerequisites":["crs_10"],"certificate":true}

Admin app 2.3 sent:
PUT /courses/crs_42
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"HTTP Fundamentals","description":"...","level":"beginner","price":149000}

Response: 200 OK
{"id":"crs_42","title":"HTTP Fundamentals","level":"beginner","price":149000,"prerequisites":[],"certificate":false}

Statement: "The server treated this PUT the way HTTP defines it, and the same edit sent as PATCH with Content-Type application/merge-patch+json and the body {\"title\":\"HTTP Fundamentals\"} would have kept the prerequisites and the certificate setting."
